===Etymology===
Diminutive of {{m|de|Eichhorn}}, folk etymology based on {{m|de|Eiche}} and  {{m|de|Horn}}, but actually from {{etyl|goh|de}} ''[[eihhorno]]'', from {{etyl|gem-pro|de}} {{m|gem-pro|*aikwernô}}, ultimately from {{etyl|ine-pro|de}} {{m|ine-pro|*aig-||move quickly}} and {{etyl|ine-pro|de}} {{m|ine-pro|*wer-||squirrel}}.<ref>[https://www.dwds.de/wb/Eichhörnchen Eichhörnchen] in DWDS (''Digitales Wörterbuch der deutschen Sprache''</ref> Compare Dutch {{m|nl|eekhoorn}}, {{m|nl|eekhoorntje}}, West Frisian {{m|fy|iikhoarntsje}}, Middle English {{m|en|aquerne}}, Danish {{m|da|egern}}, Norwegian {{m|no|ekorn}}, Swedish {{m|sv|ekorre}}, Icelandic {{m|is|íkorni}}.

